messages:
carla: quick q — our wasm (rust->wasm) client is intermittently failing JSON.parse on SSE. looks like chunks split multibyte chars + auth refresh causing small fragments. anyone seen this pattern?

denis: seen similar when a rate limiter stalls the stream and the decoder gets a partial UTF-8 sequence. parser throws on attempt to JSON.parse. :eyes:

susan: do you have an example chunk stream? is server sending ndjson or one object per stream event?

carla: server uses event: message + data: <json> (ndjson-style). logs show 2 things: auth refresh (401->reconnect) and our client rate limiter pausing reads for ~30-50ms then resuming. repro log snippet: 

```
data: {"msg":"start","id":1}\n
data: {"partial":"\uD83D\uDE"  <-- truncated emoji + end-of-chunk
(reconnect)
```

carla: then JSON.parse on that concatenation fails because of broken surrogate pair.

denis: yep. two approaches that worked for us: 1) incremental UTF-8 aware decoder that keeps incomplete bytes across chunks, or 2) treat SSE data as NDJSON and reassemble by newline boundaries without assuming utf8 char-aligned chunks.

tim: for rust+wasm, try using encoding_rs or use TextDecoder with streaming in JS glue: `let td = new TextDecoder(); text += td.decode(chunk, {stream: true});` that will preserve split multibyte sequences. (WASM linear memory -> JS Uint8Array).

susan: also watch auth refresh: if you reconnect mid-object, server might resend partial event. we added a small debounce on reconnects so the client drains the pending buffer before starting new connection. that reduced partials drastically.

carla: nice. does anyone have a tiny reassembly snippet we can drop in?

denis: simple JS outline that worked for us (can be ported to wasm glue):

```
let buf = '';
function onChunk(bytes) {
  buf += td.decode(bytes, {stream: true});
  let nl;
  while ((nl = buf.indexOf('\n')) !== -1) {
    const line = buf.slice(0, nl).trim();
    buf = buf.slice(nl + 1);
    if (!line) continue;
    try { const obj = JSON.parse(line); handle(obj); } catch (e) { /* incomplete -> keep in buf */ buf = line + '\n' + buf; break; }
  }
}
```

denis: key is using streaming TextDecoder so surrogate halves don't create parse errors.

carla: great — we'll add that to the wasm glue and add a tiny backoff on reconnects + a read-window for the rate limiter so it yields but drains.

susan: fwiw, we also added a metric: "sse.partial_json_errors" -> alerts if >5/min. helped catch regressions.

infra-bot: canary deploy at 2026-03-17T11:32Z for client-lib patch (carla/wasm-sserepair). :rocket:

carla: thanks all, will push a PR later today and tag y'all for review. :thumbsup:
